From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:16:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: misc: onboard_usb_dev: Add the AICSemi AIC8800D80

The AIC8800D80 WiFi and Bluetooth module sits behind a hub on boards
like the Radxa Cubie A7S. It needs a supply and a CHIP_EN pin that is
released after the supply is stable. Without an entry nothing powers it
before the hub enumerates the port.

Add it as a non-hub device with one supply and a reset GPIO. The delay
between supply and reset release is the longest one of the existing
entries, it has not been measured.

The module enumerates as a69c:8d80 and, once its firmware is loaded,
again as a69c:8d81. Add both to the USB ID table, so the USB device is
bound in either state and stays powered in suspend when it is a wakeup
source.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the driver switches on
the supply and releases CHIP_EN, only then the module enumerates on
port 1 of the hub, and the driver binds its USB device. The ID after the
firmware download is not tested, the firmware loader is not in mainline.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.c | 3 +++
 drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.h | 9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.c b/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.c
index 11508ed4df25..87ab8283366b 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.c
@@ -564,6 +564,7 @@ static struct platform_driver onboard_dev_driver = {
 
 /************************** USB driver **************************/
 
+#define VENDOR_ID_AICSEMI	0xa69c
 #define VENDOR_ID_BISON		0x5986
 #define VENDOR_ID_CORECHIPS	0x3431
 #define VENDOR_ID_CYPRESS	0x04b4
@@ -650,6 +651,8 @@ static void onboard_dev_usbdev_disconnect(struct usb_device *udev)
 }
 
 static const struct usb_device_id onboard_dev_id_table[] = {
+	{ USB_DEVICE(VENDOR_ID_AICSEMI, 0x8d80) }, /* AIC8800D80 WiFi/BT, firmware download */
+	{ USB_DEVICE(VENDOR_ID_AICSEMI, 0x8d81) }, /* AIC8800D80 WiFi/BT */
 	{ USB_DEVICE(VENDOR_ID_BISON, 0x1198) }, /* Bison Electronics Inc. Integrated Camera */
 	{ USB_DEVICE(VENDOR_ID_CORECHIPS, 0x6241) }, /* SL6341 2.0 HUB */
 	{ USB_DEVICE(VENDOR_ID_CORECHIPS, 0x6341) }, /* SL6341 3.0 HUB */
diff --git a/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.h b/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.h
index 3523f8f8a149..28be353f1130 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.h
@@ -127,6 +127,14 @@ static const struct onboard_dev_pdata wch_ch334_data = {
 	.is_hub = true,
 };
 
+static const struct onboard_dev_pdata aicsemi_aic8800d80_data = {
+	/* Longest delay of the entries above, not measured on hardware */
+	.reset_us = 14000,
+	.num_supplies = 1,
+	.supply_names = { "vdd" },
+	.is_hub = false,
+};
+
 static const struct onboard_dev_pdata xmos_xvf3500_data = {
 	.reset_us = 1,
 	.num_supplies = 2,
@@ -170,6 +178,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id onboard_dev_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "usb3431,6241", .data = &corechips_sl6341_data, },
 	{ .compatible = "usb3431,6341", .data = &corechips_sl6341_data, },
 	{ .compatible = "usb5986,1198", .data = &bison_intcamera_data, },
+	{ .compatible = "usba69c,8d80", .data = &aicsemi_aic8800d80_data, },
 	{}
 };
 
